## Correction (2026-10-17) — fourth run of this date: `sh dup-test.sh` 74 -> 82, by a DIFFERENT cause

A fresh-context verifier returned CONTRADICTS on PR #147 with six defects; all six
were in text or in a check this pass wrote, and all six are recorded in `FINDINGS.md`'s
fourth `## Correction (2026-10-17)` section. Fixing them moved **this** table once
more, and **not for the cause the three moves above share**:

    74 -> 82  =  one more Correction heading (+1)
              +  the WITHDRAWN-position block the widened bound now prints (+7)

The widened bound is the verifier's second finding. `dup-test.sh` derived its
edited-file list with `grep -v '^findings-log/'`, justified by a comment reading "this
PR's entire diff outside its own log directory is
`docs/11-suggested-research-areas.md`". **This PR also edits
`findings-log/2026-10-14-lane-s6-public-index/account.py`**, so that bound excused the
one other edited file the PR has and could not see a pointer into the script the PR
edits. The list is now derived from `SELF_DIR` — this pass's own log directory and
nothing else — and the subject test also matches a basename, because the prose writes
`account.py` and not the full path. With the bound correct, **two stale positions come
into scope**: `account.py:109` in live §7b and in live §8c, invalidated by this PR
editing `account.py`. They sit in sections that predate the append-only rule and may
not be edited, so they are listed in `WITHDRAWN`, matched **exact-string** so a new
position into the same file is still a hit, and **printed by the check** so the
residual is never mistaken for coverage.

**Every row below was re-run in the same pass**, from this pass's own worktree and
from inside this directory, with `2>&1 | grep -c ''` and the exit code recorded
separately:

    population 0/27   schemas 0/37   manifest 0/9   census 0/264
    self-test  0/52   dup-test 0/83   locate   0/33 kib-detector 0/53

**Only the dup-test row moved.** The other seven are unchanged at 27 / 37 / 9 / 264 /
52 / 33 / 53 — and unchanged is measured, not carried: this pass re-ran all eight.
**dup-test.sh now gives the same 83 lines and the same exit 0 whether invoked from the
repo root or from this directory**; an intermediate revision did not, because
`SELF_DIR` was derived from `dirname "$0"`, which is `.` under the second invocation
and filtered nothing. **0 requests; nothing re-probed; no vendor host touched.**

